#Problem APEX 5.1.38

## DBsubject(Calculus - single variable)
## DBchapter(Integrals)
## DBsection(Antiderivatives (without trigonometric functions))
## Institution(Valdosta State University)
## KEYWORDS(indefinite integral, 'initial value problem')
## Author(S. V. Ault)
## Level(3)
## MO(1)
## TitleText1('APEX Calculus')
## AuthorText1('Hartman')
## EditionText1('3.0')
## Section1('5.1')
## Problem1('38')

DOCUMENT();
loadMacros('PGstandard.pl', 'PGML.pl', 'PGcourse.pl');

Context('Numeric')->flags->set(tolerance => 0.01, tolType => "absolute");

$x  = random(-5, 5);
$y1 = non_zero_random(-5, 5);
$y2 = non_zero_random(-5, 5);

$f = "0";

$C1    = $y1;
$C2    = $y2 - $y1 * $x;
$f_int = Formula("$C1 x + $C2");

BEGIN_PGML
Find the function [`f(x)`] described by the given
initial value problem.
[```
  f''(x) = [$f], \qquad f'([$x]) = [$y1], \;\; f([$x]) = [$y2]
```]

[`f(x) =`] [____]{$f_int}{30}
END_PGML

BEGIN_PGML_HINT
[`  f'(x) = \int 0 \, dx = 0x + C_1 = C_1. `]  So [`f'(x) = f'([$x]) = [$y1]`].   [`  f(x) = \int [$y1] \, dx   = [$y1] x + C_2. `]  Find [`C_2`] by setting [`f([$x]) = [$y2]`]. 
END_PGML_HINT

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
Start with
[```
  f'(x) = \int 0 \, dx = 0x + C_1 = C_1.
```]   

Since [`f'([$x]) = [$y1]`], we have [`C_1 = [$y1]`].

[```
  f(x) = \int [$y1] \, dx 
  = [$y1] x + C_2.
```]

Find [`C_2`] by setting [`f([$x]) = [$y2]`].

[```
  \begin{aligned}
    [$y1]([$x]) + C_2 &= [$y2]\\
     C_2 &= [$C2]
  \end{aligned}
```]

Thus, [`f(x) = [$C1] x + [$C2]`].
END_PGML_SOLUTION
ENDDOCUMENT();   